---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Header from '@/components/layout/Header.astro'
import Main from '@/components/layout/Main.astro'
import Footer from '@/components/layout/Footer.astro'
import PageHeader from '@/components/ui/PageHeader.astro'
import NewTabIndicator from '@/components/ui/NewTabIndicator.astro'
import { PROSE_CONTENT_CLASSES } from '@/utils/prose'
---

<BaseLayout
    title="Privacy Policy"
    description="What personal data philipp.fyi collects, why it's processed, and what rights you have under the GDPR."
    ogImage="/og/privacy.png"
>
    <Header />
    <Main>
        <PageHeader eyebrow="Your data, explained" title="Privacy Policy">
            philipp.fyi collects a small amount of personal data through its
            contact form and hosting infrastructure. This page explains what's
            collected, who processes it, and how to exercise your rights.
        </PageHeader>

        <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pb-32">
            <article class={PROSE_CONTENT_CLASSES}>
                <h2>Controller</h2>
                <p>
                    Philipp Storl, based in the Chemnitz / Leipzig area,
                    Germany, is the controller responsible for the personal data
                    processed on this site (philipp.fyi). You can reach me
                    through the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>.
                </p>

                <h2>What this site collects</h2>

                <h3>Contact form</h3>
                <p>
                    When you submit the contact form, I collect your name, email
                    address, and the message you write. This data is used solely
                    to respond to your inquiry.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR, your consent, given by
                        submitting the form.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Recipient:
                        <a
                            href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/"
                            target="_blank"
                            rel="noopener noreferrer"
                            >Netlify, Inc.<NewTabIndicator
                        /></a
                        >, which stores form submissions on my behalf as a
                        processor (Netlify Forms).
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Retention: kept for as long as needed to respond to and
                        follow up on your inquiry, then deleted. You can ask me
                        to delete it sooner at any time.
                    </li>
                </ul>

                <h3>Hosting and server logs</h3>
                <p>
                    This site is hosted on Netlify. Like most hosting providers,
                    Netlify's infrastructure automatically logs technical
                    request data (for example IP address, requested URL,
                    timestamp, and user agent) for a limited time, to operate,
                    secure, and troubleshoot the site.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, my legitimate interest
                        in operating a secure, reliable website.
                    </li>
                    <li>Recipient: Netlify, Inc.</li>
                </ul>

                <h3>Performance monitoring</h3>
                <p>
                    Netlify's hosting platform includes a built-in Real User
                    Monitoring beacon, served from this domain, that reports
                    aggregate performance metrics (for example page load times)
                    to Netlify. It doesn't use cookies or any persistent
                    identifier, and isn't used for advertising or to track you
                    across other sites.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, my legitimate interest
                        in monitoring and improving site performance.
                    </li>
                    <li>Recipient: Netlify, Inc.</li>
                </ul>

                <h3>CSP violation reports</h3>
                <p>
                    This site's browser security policy asks your browser to
                    report any blocked or unexpected script/style activity. If
                    your browser sends one, it's stored (via Netlify Blobs) for
                    up to 30 days so it can be investigated, then automatically
                    deleted.
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, my legitimate interest
                        in detecting and fixing security issues.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        Recipient: Netlify, Inc. If a Slack alert channel is
                        configured, a summary of the report (including the
                        blocked/document URL and your browser's user agent) is
                        also forwarded there so I can investigate promptly.
                    </li>
                </ul>

                <h2>International data transfers</h2>
                <p>
                    Netlify, Inc. is based in the United States. Where data is
                    transferred outside the European Economic Area, Netlify
                    relies on the Standard Contractual Clauses and/or the
                    EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework as a safeguard. See
                    <a
                        href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener noreferrer"
                        >Netlify's privacy policy<NewTabIndicator
                    /></a>
                    for details.
                </p>

                <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
                <p>
                    This site doesn't use cookies and doesn't run any
                    third-party advertising or tracking scripts. The
                    performance-monitoring beacon described above uses neither.
                    Separately, this site stores exactly one preference, your
                    light/dark theme choice, in your browser's local storage.
                    That value never leaves your browser and isn't linked to you
                    personally.
                </p>

                <h2>Your rights</h2>
                <p>Under the GDPR, you have the right to:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>access the personal data I hold about you (Art. 15)</li>
                    <li>have inaccurate data corrected (Art. 16)</li>
                    <li>have your data deleted (Art. 17)</li>
                    <li>restrict how your data is processed (Art. 18)</li>
                    <li>receive your data in a portable format (Art. 20)</li>
                    <li>
                        object to processing based on legitimate interest (Art.
                        21)
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        withdraw consent at any time, without affecting
                        processing that already happened (Art. 7(3))
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <p>
                    To exercise any of these, use the
                    <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>. You also have the
                    right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority, in
                    particular the
                    <a
                        href="https://www.datenschutz.sachsen.de/"
                        target="_blank"
                        rel="noopener noreferrer"
                        >Sächsische Datenschutz- und
                        Transparenzbeauftragte<NewTabIndicator
                    /></a>
                    (the data protection authority for Saxony, Germany, where
                    I'm based), or the authority in your own country of
                    residence.
                </p>

                <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
                <p>
                    I'll update this page if what this site collects or how it's
                    processed changes. Last updated: September 15, 2026.
                </p>
            </article>
        </div>
    </Main>
    <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
